a could ease 'trust and integration' concerns driving the AI Software & Agents theme."],"risks":["Operating margin is already decelerating slightly YoY (-55bps), and further compression would break the 'quality compounding' part of the thesis.","Stock remains in a technical downtrend (below 200dma, negative MACD) and could continue to underperform even as fundamentals hold, if the market keeps discounting AI disruption risk.","Macro regime is split nearly evenly across four scenarios (27.7% Goldilocks, 27.6% Contraction), leaving meaningful tail risk to a Stagflation/Contraction combination that would hurt high-multiple software despite Adobe's cheap absolute valuation."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (from 12.0%)","ROIC falls below 45% (from 59.4%)","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.5 pts (from -0.5 pts)","Technology rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (from +68)","Combined Stagflation + Contraction regime probability exceeds 55% (currently ~50% combined)","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45 (from 64.0)"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Cloud infrastructure providers (AWS, Azure, GCP) hosting Adobe's Creative Cloud and AI compute workloads benefit from continued platform growth.","AI chip and inference providers (e.g., Nvidia, AMD) indirectly benefit if Adobe scales generative AI features (Firefly) requiring more compute.","Enterprise systems integrators and creative agencies that help large customers embed Adobe's AI tools into workflows could see incremental demand if 'trust and integration' friction described in the theme thesis is the binding constraint."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue growth is 12.0% vs 11.5% prior quarter","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"ROIC is 59.4% with incremental ROIC of 148.9%","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E is at the 5th percentile and EV/Sales at the 0